nesting filthy oxes gollum a miserable  wretched creature from the works of  j.r.r tolkien who's easy to hate and  just as easy to pity after being a side  character in both bilbo and frodo's  journeys and all of the adaptations of  them he's now the main character in his  own game the lord of the rings gollum  now as gamespot's certified lord of the  rings expert i recently attended a  hands-off preview event for the game i  saw a big chunk of gameplay and had the  opportunity to ask the development team  some questions so here are seven things  i learned the lord of the rings golem  takes place roughly parallel to the  events of the early chapters of the  fellowship of the ring as a little recap  in the hobbit gollum loses the one ring  or should i say the one ring loses  gollum only for it to be picked up by  bilbo baggins and his hands is in the  time between the hobbit and the lord of  the rings gollum is desperate to find  the ring once again and so he eventually  leaves the cave which he's called home  for a couple of hundred years to try and  track down bilbo through merkwood but  the trail has gone cold he eventually  turned to go to mordor where he was  captured by sauron's forces and tortured  into giving up the name of the one  ring's new carrier and where they could  be found  after leaving mordor aragorn captured  gollum and gandalf interrogated him to  find out what sauron knows now there's a  lot to play around with here in terms of  story but it won't cross over with the  fellowship's quest too much allegedly  ending somewhere around the mines of  moria the dev team also confirmed that  there wouldn't be flashbacks to before  he found the ring this is very much  gollum's game so who knows if we'll even  actually meet up with frodo and the rest  of the fellowship let's go over gollum's  abilities then true to tolkien's  description he is a sneaky stealthy but  very athletic boy who prefers to avoid  head-on confrontation but can still do  some damage when cornered as a stealth  action game prepare to do a lot of  sneaking as well as a lot of climbing  the levels of the game that i saw in  action kirith ongol and merkwood were  both filled to the brim with climbing  and platforming puzzles gollum can leap  over large gaps as well as climb various  formations in the environment like vines  and rock faces but when he's hanging on  by just his arms he has a stamina bar  that begins to deplete when it comes to  stealth just like practically every  modern game with stealth elements  there's a kind of detective mode that  you can activate it's called golem  vision which  i don't remember that from the book but  in the gameplay that i saw in kirith  ungol golem was hiding from two orcs and  activated the golem vision and it showed  not only where the orcs were in the  environment but it also showed hiding  spots and sort of the general direction  of your objective combat then you can  knock out enemies but it's incredibly  risky first of all unlike most modern  stealth games enemies make noise when  attacked and taking them down takes a  while so you really need to be sure that  the coast is clear you also need to make  sure you even have enough stamina to  finish the job so honestly sneaking  might just be your best bet gollum  obviously doesn't have a huge weapon  wheel full of things to use but he can  pick up small items like rocks to throw  and cause a distraction that way  there will also be boss-like encounters  but apparently they will be more puzzly  than combat driven we've talked a lot  about gollum but we haven't even  mentioned smeagle the other main  character in this game so to speak  before being corrupted by the one ring  gollum was a hobbit-like creature called  smeagle his hundreds of years with the  ring changed him into the figure we know  of him today but over that time his  personality cracked for lack of a better  word the golem personality is full of  hatred hatred for the elves himself and  despite craving its return even the ring  smeagle on the other hand is the more  optimistic naive side who remembers what  it was like to feel emotions like  happiness and love as a result they  argue and in the game this is presented  as a choice-driven mechanic either side  with gollum or with smeagol siding with  one strengthens that persona affecting  other things in the game such as the  fate of some characters as well as  certain situations you stumble across  but it doesn't give either side unique  abilities the dev team said that this  wouldn't make sense law wise because  it's two personalities yes but they are  within the same body the choice i saw in  action was gollum arguing with smeagol  over whether or not to kill and eat a  bug now obviously that's not a huge  decision in the grand scheme of things  but it did offer a really nice character  moment when the smeagol side won it  showed how pitiful and lonely he is and  honestly it had it had huge it was pity  that stayed bilbo's hand energy we  obviously know that gollum is going to  be in the game but which other  recognizable faces from tolkien's vast  middle earth can we expect a good few as  it turns out in kirath ongol there are  numerous references to shelob from  webbing everywhere to gollum mentioning  her name outright i also saw a cutscene  featuring a fel beast the big winged  creatures that the nazgul ride so i  wouldn't be surprised if they show up  too throughout the gameplay i saw gollum  was having audio  flashes i'm unsure if they were  flashbacks or flash forwards to his  interrogation with gandalf later on in  the gameplay that i saw we ended up in  merckwood and gandalf and thranduil were  there discussing the one ring and gollum  now given that aragorn is the person who  brings gollum to merkwood i wouldn't be  surprised if he showed up too the  development team has also introduced new  characters there was an elf called mel  who was in the gameplay that i saw  although i didn't get to see mel i just  heard her voice she has also been  imprisoned in thranduil's halls and  gollum strikes an uncanny friendship  with them to the point where he's even  trying to rescue her from the prison  that she's in if you're on the hunt for  more easter eggs and references to the  lord of the rings apparently they will  be bountiful and there will be  collectibles that will definitely appeal  to tolkien fans in terms of locations  i've mentioned a few already we'll  definitely be exploring kirith ongol and  merkwood the devs also name-dropped  barador during the presentation which  makes a lot of sense given that that's  where gollum is taken when he's captured  by sauron you can also explore gollum's  cave where he has a bunch of drawings  that he's done on the rocks and on the  walls  of events in his life if you choose to  interact with them you get these kind of  nice character moments where both gollum  and smeagol will weigh in on their  interpretation of the events a big  question when it comes to tie in media  is the lord of the rings gollum cannon i  can confirm it is the development team  daedalic struck a deal with middle-earth  enterprises who ultimately have to  approve everything to make sure it's  accurate to what j.r.r tolkien wrote  while we know a little about gollum's  journey at this point in the story there  is still plenty that's been left  unwritten and so the development team  have gone in and wrote their own story  in terms of the aesthetic gollum  obviously doesn't look like the one from  peter jackson's film trilogy nor is he  played by andy serkis in the lord of the  rings golem he is played by wayne  forrester a british voice actor who has  been in a bunch of things but most  recently he was one of the male  protagonist voices in elden ring i'm not  sure who is doing the voice of gandalf  but whoever it is they are seriously  doing their best ian mckellen we  actually don't have that long to wait  until the lord of the rings golem  launches it'll be hitting playstation 4  playstation 5 xbox one xbox series x and  s and pc on september 1st a whole day  before the new lord of the rings tv  series the rings of power premieres on  amazon prime the game is confirmed to be  coming to nintendo switch later this  year but there's no release date just  yet there won't be a collector's edition  but there will be some kind of digital  deluxe edition with some more bells and  whistles if that's your thing and as  someone with the extended editions of  all the movies yes including the hobbit  trilogy that's that's probably me  anyway that's everything i learned about  the lord of the rings gollum from that  recent preview event that i went to if  you have any more questions about it  make sure to drop them in the comments  below i will be going through them and  answering as best as i can or you can  come find me on twitter i'm at lucy  james games for more on the lord of the  rings gollum as well as any upcoming  lord of the rings stuff  keep your eyes peeled to gamespot and  gamespot universe
 

